    "result": "I implemented `check_password` in `solution.py` following the spec. I did not run it or write any tests, as instructed.\n\n- **Type check:** it raises `TypeError` if `password` or `username` isn't a `str`.\n- **Rule order:** it returns the violated codes in the required order: LENGTH, CLASSES, USERNAME, REPEAT, BLOCKLIST.\n- **LENGTH:** violated unless `len(password)` is 12 to 64.\n- **CLASSES:** counts ASCII lowercase, ASCII uppercase, ASCII digits, and everything else (including `é`). It flags a password with fewer than 3 classes.\n- **USERNAME:** only applies when the username has 3 or more characters, and does a lowercase substring match.\n- **REPEAT:** checks for three identical consecutive characters, case-sensitively.\n- **BLOCKLIST:** flags a lowercase equality match with any lowercased entry. It skips non-string entries and treats a `None` blocklist as empty, which the spec doesn't mention.",
